# Agent continuity (MANDATORY — every session)

Read first: `docs/AGENT_CONTINUITY.md`, `docs/AGENT_OPERATIONS.md`, `docs/USER_PREFERENCES.md`.

## Session start (before any code change)

1. `git fetch origin master` (or `main`) and confirm you branch from latest default branch.
2. Read `docs/AGENT_STATUS.md` manual notes + open PRs for your workstream.
3. Search git history for prior work on the same feature (`git log --oneline --all --grep=…`, `git branch -a --contains …`).
4. If an older `cursor/*` branch or open PR already implements part of the task, **continue that branch/PR** — do not re-implement on a fresh branch.
5. Run `./scripts/agent-continuity-check.sh` when resuming work or when the user says "continue / folytasd".

## Session end (before marking task done — NO EXCEPTIONS)

A task is **NOT done** until all of the following are true:

1. **Committed + pushed** on `cursor/<workstream>-<task>-<suffix>`.
2. **PR opened or updated** targeting `master` (use ManagePullRequest; not draft forever unless blocked).
3. **Merged to `master`** when the change is approved / CI green / user said proceed — agent merges, user does not click merge.
4. **Deployed** when the workstream has a live service (`docs/AGENT_OPERATIONS.md`).
5. **Agent log written**: `docs/agent-log/<workstream>/YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ-<slug>.md` using `docs/agent-log/HANDOFF_TEMPLATE.md`.
6. **Manual note** added to `docs/AGENT_STATUS.md` if the workstream state changed.
7. **Handoff message to user** (Hungarian): branch, PR link, merge commit, deploy version/URL, rollback pointer.

## Forbidden outcomes

- Leaving working code only on a `cursor/*` branch without merge.
- Rebuilding a feature from scratch when an unmerged branch/PR already exists.
- Ending with "open a PR when ready" / "merge when you want" — **you** merge unless user explicitly forbids deploy.
- Large refactors without backup (`docs/backups/` or `backups/`) and rollback notes (`docs/ROLLBACK.md`).

## Rollback

Every live-impacting change must document how to undo it in the agent log + `docs/ROLLBACK.md` section for that workstream.

## New agent / long context

If context is large or the user starts a new agent: **stop and hand off** using the template; never silently drop unmerged work.
